<title>FRANCE: Alcatel signs $225 mln Indonesia GSM deal.</title>
<headline>Alcatel signs $225 mln Indonesia GSM deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Alcatel Alsthom said on Thursday it had signed a deal with Indonesian cellular network operator Satelindo, winning Alcatel GSM orders worth $225 million.  </p>
<p>It said in a statement the deal meant that Alcatel had won firm orders from the private Indonesian operator, one worth $70 million for the GSM network extension in Java and one worth $150 million for a further GSM development phase in Jakarta and other areas.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
